# notify-ui environment variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in values for local development.
# Never commit .env.local or any file with real secrets.

# notify-ui's own authenticated calls to notify-api (T15,
# specs/005-notification-center) go through the shared `shell/session`
# module's `getNotifyBaseUrl()` / `apiFetch` (VITE_NOTIFY_API_URL lives in
# shell/.env.example, not here) — same pattern admin-ui uses for the auth
# service's admin API.

# SHELL_REMOTE_URL — build-time dev default for the shell's remoteEntry.js,
# read by vite.config.ts (process.env, NOT import.meta.env — this is a
# Node-side config value, not a browser-side Vite env var). notify-ui
# consumes `shell/session` + `shell/tokens.css` from this URL as a Module
# Federation remote (ADR-0006). Same pattern as admin-ui/refund-ui/
# estimai-ui's own SHELL_REMOTE_URL. Defaults to the shell's pinned local-dev
# port (http://localhost:5173/remoteEntry.js) when unset — override only when
# pointing at a non-default shell instance (e.g. a deployed preview URL).
# SHELL_REMOTE_URL=http://localhost:5173/remoteEntry.js
